+
+# fix-server-name-ipv6
+
+## Why
+`app.run()` splits `SERVER_NAME` on its first colon, which turns a bracketed IPv6 literal into an invalid host and port.
+
+## What
+- Parse bracketed IPv6 `SERVER_NAME` host:port values without treating an address colon as the host/port delimiter.
+- Cover the behavior in the existing `app.run()` configuration test.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] With `SERVER_NAME="[::1]:8080"` and no explicit host or port, `app.run()` passes host `::1` and port `8080` to the development server — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q`
+- [x] Existing hostname and port-zero defaults remain unchanged — check: `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests/test_basic.py -q`
